    <string name="ig_the_full_privacy_policy_is_coming_soon_preferences_stay_local_" formatted="false">Usage Access reads Android app usage records for statistics, limits, and session timing. Turning it off removes system usage from stats and suspends verified timing.\n\nAccessibility detects app switches, shows background Intent Check and expiry prompts, and can return to Home when you tap Finish. Turning it off disables that detection and the accessibility overlay.\n\nDisplay over other apps provides an expiry prompt when the accessibility overlay is unavailable. Without either overlay, expiry can use a notification. Notifications deliver Intent Check, expiry, and limit reminders. Turning notifications off stops those alerts.\n\nManaged apps, intentions you enter, sessions, limits, and consent are stored locally. Only the language preference is eligible for Android cloud backup and device transfer under this version’s rules.</string>
