    <string name="ig_desktop_window_disclosure">IntentGate uses Accessibility to observe foreground window changes and app package names, including when you leave a managed app. It uses this signal with Android usage records to show its own Intent Check and expiry prompts in the background. Tapping Finish on the expiry overlay returns to the Home screen.\n\nThe service discards raw window events and does not read screen text, messages, or passwords. Intent Check requests and confirmed sessions are stored locally and excluded from this version’s backup and transfer rules. You can turn off the service in Android settings.</string>
